# Architecture

Layer boundary, public contract, data schema, and external integration get a recommendation from the matching architect first. Architects do not edit files.

Do not replace a decision already in project docs. If there is no decision and structure depends on it, stop and ask.

Repeat the project's existing pattern. Do not add a new shell, library, or database without a direct ask. Do not create an empty catch-all library. A module's public entry only lists what the project already treats as public — no implementation dump.

A project rule may tighten work in its repo. It does not override core bans: models, secrets, foreign files, cloud Graphify.
